#*
 Whole-page Velocity render error.

 What a reader gets on a public weblog whose template would not load. It is
 sent as HTTP 500 and never cached (VelocityRenderer.renderedError and
 RenderingServletUtils.renderAndFlush; RenderErrorStatusTest). It shows no
 exception detail -- that goes to the server log -- only the same calm card,
 palette and wording as pressroom-ui/errors/error.jsp, in light and dark.
 Pinned by VelocityErrorTemplateTest.
*#
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title>$text.get("errorPage.title")</title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; --paper: #F7F9F9; --surface: #FFFFFF; --ink: #17262A;
        --ink-soft: #5A6E72; --line: #DCE4E4; --accent: #0F6E68; }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --paper: #131C1C; --surface: #1A2626; --ink: #DCE7E5;
          --ink-soft: #8FA5A2; --line: #2A3838; --accent: #4FB3AA; }
      }
      body { margin: 0; padding: 4rem 1rem; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
        font-family: "IBM Plex Sans", system-ui, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; }
      .box { max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; }
      .code { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); }
      h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; }
      p { margin: 0 0 .75rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
      a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
    </style>
</head>
<!-- error-page -->
<body>
    <main class="box">
        <p class="code">500</p>
        <h1>$text.get("errorPage.title")</h1>
        <p>$text.get("errorPage.message")</p>
        <p><a href="$url.absoluteSite">$utils.escapeHTML($config.siteName)</a></p>
    </main>
</body>
</html>